Final Suggestions for your Scenario:

1.  Atomic Updates: When you update Hive, make sure you update the specific
    index in the list so you don't accidentally overwrite new data with old
    data.
2.  Unique Time: Use the time (milliseconds) as the unique key for every API
    call. This is the only way to prevent duplicates on the server if the
    Background and Foreground processes ever run at the same time.
3.  Location Filter: When sending locations during Clock-Out, make sure you only
    send locations where time >= clock_in_time and time <= clock_out_time. This
    prevents sending the 27th's location data during the 28th's shift.

Conclusion: Your plan is very good. If you implement a "Sync Lock" (to prevent
two processes from running at once) and "Server-side checks" (using the
timestamp), your data will be 100% safe and duplicate-free.


